# Chart colour

Decide first whether colour identifies a source or shows a quantity. In the maintained household charts, a categorical colour identifies a source or device. It must not change because you added another source, hid a series or switched the theme colour. For example, the dishwasher keeps its colour whether or not the oven is shown. Light and Dark remain separate display modes.

The [machine-readable contract](../reference/chart-colours.json) and the repository module `design-system/chart-colours.mjs` are the shared authority for the theme, the native Energy adapter and the [working examples](../components/chart-examples.html). Do not define another palette inside a chart or demonstration.


## Apply data guidance

[Data visualisation](brand-data.html) owns how to show a result, a comparison or uncertainty. The series colours on this page and the [maintained Energy chart specification](../components/charts.html) are the operational contract. The quantitative scales below are worked references for newly written graphics. They do not change native Home Assistant charts or maps.


